    reg {
        name = "JPGD clock and soft reset control register";
        desc = "Vendor sequences (hi3520D_jpegd.ko; hi3520D_sys.ko SYS_HAL_JpgdClkEn / SYS_HAL_JpgdResetSel touch only these two bits, the JPGD module ioremaps this register itself): module init writes 0, then sets bit 1 (clock on), then clears bit 0 (reset released); every open of /dev/jpeg and the reset ioctl set bit 0, poll JPGD_START bit 1 until it reads 0, then clear bit 0; module exit clears bit 1 (clock off). The vendor U-Boot decoder does the same with clock on, reset asserted, poll, reset released. The reset value 0x3 (clock on, reset asserted) is from the data sheet. Source: vendor module hi3520D_jpegd.ko (JPEG_DRV_K_ModInit 0xaac, jpg_osr_ioctl 0x378, JPEG_DRV_ModExit 0x9fc) and hi3520D_sys.ko (SYS_HAL_JpgdClkEn 0x50bc, SYS_HAL_JpgdResetSel 0x5088), confidence HIGH, word-checked: yes; Not verified on hardware.";

