    reg {
        name = "SATA related clock and soft reset control register";
        desc = "
        Clock gates, reference clock select and the eight soft resets of the AHCI SATA host at 0x10080000 and its PHY (DS 14.7.5, `datasheet.txt` lines 57113-57260). Reset bits are asserted (1) after power-on
        by the hardware default of 0; the bring-up order is: PERI_CRG45 bit 11 = 0 (150 MHz reference), deassert `hrst_sata_s` (bit 1), deassert `rst_sataphy_s` (bit 0), program the PHY registers, pulse
        `rst_sataphy_s`, then deassert `rst_sata_s` (2), `rst_tx0_s` (3), `rst_rx0_s` (5), `rst_alive_s` (7) (and the port 1 resets 4 and 6 on Hi3520D/Hi3515A; Hi3515C has one port).
        Vendor driver (`ahci_sys_hi3520d_defconfig.c`, `HI_SATA_PERI_CRG` = CRG + 0xB4): `hi_sata_clk_open` sets bits 10, 9, 8 (`sata_cken`, `sata0_cken`, `sata1_cken`), `hi_sata_phy_clk_sel` clears bits 11
        and 12, `hi_sata_unreset` / `hi_sata_reset` clear / set bit 1, `hi_sata_phy_(un)reset` bit 0, `hi_sata_clk_(un)reset` set / clear bits 2-7 together. The SATA PHY analog options are in SYS_CTRL
        PERIPHCTRL3 / PERIPHCTRL25. The data sheet text at 14.7.5.1 says 'disable the clock by setting sata0_cken and sata1_cken to 1' (typo: 0).
         Hardware (Hi3520D V100 board, read on hardware 2026-11-08, stock U-Boot prompt after a cold boot): reads 0x00000000, i.e. all SATA clocks OFF (sata*_cken = 0) and no reset asserted. The original (Chinese) data sheet, version 02, gives the total reset value 0x0000_0000 (sata_cken, sata0_cken, sata1_cken = 0); the 0x0000_0700 'clocks on' value came from the machine translation and was wrong. Linux must enable the clocks before touching the SATA block (the SATA host registers were not read for that reason).";

        enum PERI_CRG45_cko_alive_cksel_enum {
            INTERNAL_50_MHZ = 0x0 { desc = "internal 50 MHz CRG clock"; };
            CKO_ALIVE_CLOCK = 0x1 { desc = "cko_alive clock of the SATA PHY"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "cko_alive_cksel";
            encode = PERI_CRG45_cko_alive_cksel_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } cko_alive_cksel[12:12];

        enum PERI_CRG45_sata_clk_sel_enum {
            V_150_MHZ_CLOCK = 0x0 { desc = "150 MHz clock"; };
            V_50_MHZ_CLOCK = 0x1 { desc = "50 MHz clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "sata_clk_sel";
            encode = PERI_CRG45_sata_clk_sel_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } sata_clk_sel[11:11];

        enum PERI_CRG45_sata_cken_enum {
            DISABLE = 0x0 { desc = "disabled"; };
            ENABLE = 0x1 { desc = "enabled"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "sata_cken";
            encode = PERI_CRG45_sata_cken_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } sata_cken[10:10];

